      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "Label": "UNLABELLED",
          "content": "Clonidine is an alpha2-adrenergic agonist with analgetic properties. Due to its side-effects, the drug is administered via the epidural or spinal route. A literature search yielded nine controlled studies on clonidine as a supplemental drug in the epidural or spinal treatment of cancer pain. These studies were systematically reviewed to evaluate the evidence of efficacy in patients with cancer pain."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "Despite weak evidence, clonidine may be a useful adjunct in epidural or spinal morphine therapy of cancer pain."
        }
      ]},
